WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Okay guys, in this problem we have another quick concept question being asked of us.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.560
So which of the following statements is true about the footings in the cantilevered structure

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.400
shown?

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.920
So we can see that we have a cantilevered structure with footing 1, footing 2, a load applied

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.199
on the right hand side at the top, and a wind load.

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:31.160
So the Question is, for the list of options we can select would be, footing 1 will

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:38.460
be subjected to uplift loading, footing 2 will be subjective to compressive loading, footing

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:46.079
1 will be subjected to compressive loading, footing 2 will be subjected to uplift loading,

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:51.700
both footings will be subjected to uplift loading, or both footings will be subjected to

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.640
compressive loading,

00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:00.079
And so if we're looking at the way that the force is going to be applied on this structure,

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:09.640
it's going to cause a rotation this direction essentially.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.400
So this footing is going to be subjected to an uplift force, while this footing is going

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.719
to be subjected to a compressive force.

00:01:17.719 --> 00:01:22.079
So our answer in this case is just going to be the first one here.

00:01:22.079 --> 00:01:23.319
And that's it.

00:01:23.319 --> 00:01:28.399
If you didn't know this answer, you could look back at various structural analysis

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:33.799
questions or basic static questions, which might help you to study.

00:01:33.799 --> 00:01:37.639
And if you don't know an answer on the test, you can always leave it blank and come back

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:39.639
to it later if you have time to guess.
